+### Prose Claim
+
+Header.Relations is optional. When present, it stores the Atom’s outgoing direct Relation facts about the Atom itself. The Atom is the Host of those facts; its active Subject identifies the focus of its content and is not the Host merely because it is named there. Store the Atom’s outgoing IS_CONTAINED_BY value only in Header.Container, never as a second fact under Header.Relations. Inverse aliases are reverse-view names of their canonical Relation and are not stored as separate direct facts.
